# Tailscale auth key.
#
# Generate one in the Tailscale admin console:
#   https://login.tailscale.com/admin/settings/keys
#   -> "Generate auth key"
#
# This is NOT derivable locally; `openssl rand` cannot produce one.
# Treat it as a secret: it can add nodes to your tailnet.
#
# Recommended key settings:
#   - Reusable:        off (a single-use key is safer)
#   - Pre-approved:    off (let the device appear in the admin console)
#   - Ephemeral:       off (you want this node to stay up)
#   - Expiry:          the shortest window that suits your deploy
#
# Copy this file to .env and fill in the real key, then: chmod 600 .env
TS_AUTHKEY=
